          "title": "You'll want to know: आसनम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आसनम् (āsanam) — \"a seat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Having met the guest at the door, you offer an आसनम् (āsanam) — a seat. The root means \"to sit\", and the ending makes it the thing you sit on."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English borrowed the word without the furniture: an āsana in yoga is a posture, a way of being seated. Both senses live in the one Sanskrit word, and the ordinary one is the older. Neuter -अम्, like द्वारम् (dvāram) before it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The second step of a welcome, and a third borrowed word restored."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
