          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पुष्पम् (puṣpam) — \"a flower\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पुष्पम् (puṣpam) is a flower. Its root means \"to bloom, to thrive, to nourish\", so the word names the opening rather than the petals."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already have फलम्, the fruit, and now the flower that precedes it — and in Sanskrit the pair puṣpa-phala travels together as a set phrase, flower-and-fruit, the way English says bricks and mortar. Neuter -अम्, like फलम् itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A flower to set beside the fruit you already had."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
