          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माला (mālā) — \"a garland\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Threaded, the flowers become a माला (mālā) — a garland, put over the head of a guest of honour, and also the string of beads counted through in prayer. English borrowed the second sense as mala."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its own history is unsettled: no agreed cousin outside India, like केशः and अलम् before it. Feminine, ending in -आ, like यात्रा and माता."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A third word with no proven travels, and a garland made of the last one."
            }
          ]
        },
